+# FlashStates on Ascend 910B — vLLM 0.32.0 port
+
+This branch backports the **hybrid-state frontier checkpoint** feature of
+[FlashStates](https://github.com/FutureMLS-Lab/FlashStates) to **vLLM v0.32.0**
+for Ascend 910B, on top of the `vllm-ascend` nightly image
+(`quay.io/ascend/vllm-ascend:nightly-releases-v0.32.0rc`, vLLM 0.32.0 +
+vllm-ascend 0.19.1rc2).
+
+Upstream source: `FutureMLS-Lab/vllm@3cfd432` (based on vLLM v0.33.0,
+24,642 lines / 114 files). This port keeps the Python scheduler/KV-cache
+logic and leaves the CUDA-only kernels out.
+
+## Supported
+
+- `--mamba-frontier-checkpoint`: keep a finished request's recurrent state at
+  its exact end (inside a block) and at the last block boundary its output
+  crossed; the next turn resumes there.
+- `--prefix-cache-eviction gds` + `--prefill-cost-coefficients` +
+  `--prefix-cache-leaf-last` / `--prefix-cache-leaf-idle-seconds`: evict
+  hybrid states whole by prefill seconds saved per block.
+- Requirements: `--enable-prefix-caching --mamba-cache-mode align`,
+  Model Runner V2 (`VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1`),
+  `--prefix-cache-retention-interval 0`, no context parallelism,
+  no KV cache events (unless recovery-unit events are on).
+
+## Not ported
+
+| Feature | Reason |
+| --- | --- |
+| `mamba_prefill_export` | needs FlashKDA / FlashInfer GDN CUDA kernels (`csrc/flashkda_export`, `vllm/third_party/flashinfer_gdn`) |
+| `mamba_spec_state_layout=compact` | needs CUDA + Triton Mamba backend |
+| Mooncake store frontier (`frontier_write_through`) | Mooncake store frontier protocol not adapted |
+| GDN export path (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) | CUDA-only export kernels |
+
+Keep `--mamba-prefill-export` off; the scheduler refuses it when the backend
+cannot write prefill checkpoints.
+
+## Ascend-specific changes
+
+1. `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/input_batch.py`: add
+   `prefill_checkpoint_positions: dict[str, int] | None = None`.
+   `mamba_hybrid.py` reads it unconditionally; without the field MRV2 raises
+   `AttributeError` at runtime (even when export is off).
+2. `vllm/v1/core/hybrid_checkpoint/manager.py` `layout_groups`:
+   - classify managers with `isinstance` so subclasses such as
+     `AscendCircularBufferManager(CircularBufferManager)` are treated as rings;
+   - skip `KpoolTailManager` (`FullAttentionManager` subclass) — Ascend
+     GLM5next's per-request indexer K-pool tail, with
+     `prefix_cacheable=False` and `find_longest_cache_hit` always empty.
+     The frontier's main indexer pages are still checkpointed; the tail is
+     rebuilt per request. Validating this on real weights is a remaining task.
+3. `vllm/v1/worker/utils.py` keeps the view-geometry dedup for
+   `copy_kv_cache_blocks_inplace`, which matters for hybrid models where
+   attention and Mamba state views share one allocation.
+
+## Running on Ascend
+
+```bash
+# 8×910B4, GLM-5.3-Flash W8A8 (311 GB), TP8
+docker run -d --name fs-full --net=host --ipc=host --privileged \
+  --device=/dev/davinci0 ... --device=/dev/davinci7 \
+  --device=/dev/davinci_manager --device=/dev/devmm_svm --device=/dev/hisi_hdc \
+  -v /usr/local/Ascend/driver:/usr/local/Ascend/driver \
+  -v /usr/local/Ascend/firmware:/usr/local/Ascend/firmware \
+  -v /usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/sbin -v /usr/local/dcmi:/usr/local/dcmi \
+  -v /etc/hccn.conf:/etc/hccn.conf -v /etc/ascend_install.info:/etc/ascend_install.info \
+  -v <this-repo>:/vllm-workspace/vllm \
+  -e ASCEND_RT_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 \
+  -e VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1 \
+  quay.io/ascend/vllm-ascend:nightly-releases-v0.32.0rc \
+  vllm serve /data02/GLM-5.3-Flash-w8a8-b0829 \
+    --trust-remote-code --enable-prefix-caching \
+    --mamba-cache-mode align --mamba-frontier-checkpoint \
+    --max-model-len 8192 --max-num-seqs 4 --tensor-parallel-size 8 \
+    --enforce-eager --prefix-cache-eviction lru
+```
+
+For a functional test without loading the (old-format) tiny checkpoint, add
+`--load-format dummy` and point `--model` at a GLM5next config directory.
+
+## Measured (GLM-5.3-Flash W8A8, TP8, 8K, 4 seqs, eager)
+
+- `/health` 200; 311 GB / 85 shards load in ~8–10 min.
+- Two-turn test (18-token second prompt): frontier serves **12 tokens/turn**,
+  `prefix_cache_frontier_hits_total = 24`.
+- Frontier off vs on: uncached prompt tokens **18 → 6 (−66.7%)**, cache hit
+  rate **0% → 66.7%**; total latency 1.97/1.98 s vs 1.99/1.92 s (no measurable
+  difference at 18 tokens — decode dominates).
+- HBM ~60.7/64 GB per card at 8192 context / 4 seqs; 32K or 1M context is not
+  feasible on 910B4 without reducing concurrency/context.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- Output-level A/B correctness is confounded by model nondeterminism
+  (MoE / sparse-attention kernels): the same prompt on the same server can
+  produce different 8-token continuations across runs. The first token is
+  stable; CPU state-level tests (`tests/v1/core/hybrid_checkpoint/`) pass.
+  A deterministic-kernel or logits-level comparison is the next step.
+- The included CPU suite is the four portable files (checkpoint graph,
+  frontier checkpoints, GDS eviction, recovery-unit events; 51 tests).
+  Speculative-frontier and prefill-export tests are omitted because those
+  CUDA-only paths are not ported.
+- The K-pool tail is not included in frontier checkpoints (see above).
+- No long-context / 48-session benchmark yet; the paper's 3.14× prefill /
+  3.02× decode numbers are B200, NVFP4, 1M context, 48 sessions and are not
+  directly comparable to 910B4 / W8A8 / 8K / 4 seqs.
